## Context

0151 exit criteria require: (1) maximal threat model documented with supply-chain
framing, (2) an AI-assisted red-team checklist that has run once with documented
cadence, (3) both opsec tiers documented with a verification cluestick for users.
Today the threat model lives only in the ticket body and in
`docs/audit-infrastructure-class.md`. No red-team checklist or opsec docs exist.

## Relevant files
- `tickets/0151-security-red-team-audit.erg` — threat model source material
- `docs/audit-infrastructure-class.md` — infrastructure-class design audit
- `README.md` — needs opsec tier documentation pointer
- `docs/` — target directory for new docs

## Actions
1. Create `docs/threat-model.md` consolidating the threat model from 0151's body
   and the infrastructure-class audit. Structure: assets, threat actors, attack
   surfaces (supply-chain, update, parser/input, path/ID, secrets), severity
   multiplier, controls (shipped vs planned).

2. Create `docs/red-team-checklist.md` with:
   - Checklist items organized by attack surface (matching threat model)
   - For each: attack description, test command/procedure, expected result
   - Cadence: per release, per change to parser/update/path code
   - Process: agent runs checklist, human reviews findings, high-severity → fix ticket
   - Run the checklist once against the current binary and record results inline

3. Add opsec verification section to `README.md`:
   - Basic tier: `sha256sum tickets/erg` vs `erg version` vs signed release tag
   - Advanced tier: review `src/go/`, rebuild with `make verify`, compare
   - Gentle cluestick tone, not a nag

4. Update `docs/audit-infrastructure-class.md` to cross-reference the new docs.

## Test
```sh
# Red: docs should exist
test -f docs/threat-model.md
test -f docs/red-team-checklist.md
grep -q 'sha256sum' README.md
```

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `docs/threat-model.md` exists with supply-chain framing and severity multiplier
- [ ] `docs/red-team-checklist.md` exists with per-surface items and has been run once
- [ ] README.md documents both opsec tiers with a friendly verification pointer
- [ ] `docs/audit-infrastructure-class.md` cross-references new docs
- [ ] Findings from the initial red-team run are recorded
